--TEST--
a type alias declared inside a class renamed to a constant its owner already declares is refused, and no alias is written to resolve the clash, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Order
{
    public const int LIMIT = 10;

    type To<|>tal = int;

    public function total(): Total
    {
        return 3;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
rename to=LIMIT
--EXPECT--
refused: `Order` already has a constant named `LIMIT`.
